# Architecture integrity

## Forbidden workarounds

- Never remove, gut, or permanently skip a designed layer (overlay host, theme tokens, shared control base, public barrel) to make a demo or check pass.
- Never invent a “temporary forever” workaround that recreates a removed layer somewhere else.
- Never leave a wrong identifier in place (types, inputs, files, public API) and explain the real name in a comment. Rename it. See **`rename-not-comment.mdc`**.

## When tooling blocks the design

- Stop and propose a real fix: repair the component or types, fix or request upstream library behavior, or park behind an explicit temporary flag with a tracked follow-up.
- Prefer failing loudly or documenting a blocker over shipping a degraded architecture as if it were the target state.

## CLI ownership

- Pause whenever a CLI command is needed.
- Provide a named `npm run` (or short existing CLI) and why it is needed, then wait for the user to run it and report the result.
- Do not run terminal commands on the user's behalf.
- Do not paste inline programs as the command.
- Do not embed CLI or network workarounds in repo scripts. Full rule: **`cli-ownership.mdc`**.
